# Select the REST Client environment, then authenticate as an Admin in user_auth.http.
# Use a disposable GitHub UID that does not already exist in this app.
@testUid = wilma 

### 1. Create user (expect 200)
# @name createUser
# @note Creates a real account in the selected environment. Check testUid first.
# dob is included from the example, but the current create endpoint ignores it.
# accountType mentor creates an inactive Mentor, activated in step 1b. A Teacher or Admin can activate any
# account; a student is also activated by Google at sign-up.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{testUid}}",
  "name": "Wilma Flinstone",
  "dob": "1000-01-02",
  "accountType": "mentor"
}

### 1b. Activate the new Mentor (expect 200 and "active": true)
# @name verifyUser
# @note A new Mentor is inactive and gets 403 "Account pending verification" on protected endpoints until a Teacher or Admin verifies it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/user/{{testUid}}/verify
Accept: application/json

### 2. Read logged-in user from cookie (expect 200 and role Admin)
# @name currentUser
# This returns the authenticated Admin, not the newly created user.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/id
Accept: application/json

### 3. Read all users (expect 200 and an array containing testUid)
# @name listUsers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user
Accept: application/json

### 4. Update user (expect 200 and the updated name)
# @name updateUser
# @note Requires an Admin login to update testUid rather than the logged-in account.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/user
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{testUid}}",
  "name": "Wilma Flintstone Updated"
}

### 5. Delete user (expect 204 with no response body)
# @name deleteUser
# @note Permanently deletes testUid in the selected environment. Run only after Create succeeded for this test account.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/user
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{testUid}}"
}
